  data: {
    LLM: "Keep your 'Pope'! Save the 9 of Diamonds for a moment when an opponent is building a long sequence that you can't follow. By playing the Pope, you stop their momentum and get to lead a new sequence of your own. Also, pay attention to the trump suitâ€”winning the 'Matrimony' stake (King and Queen) is often more lucrative than finishing the round first.\n\nThe 'Stop Hand' Deduction: As cards are played, you can figure out what is in the face-down 'Stop Hand'. If a 5 of Spades is led and no one plays the 6, the 6 is definitely in the Stop Hand. This makes the 5 a permanent 'Stop' for the rest of the game. Use this knowledge to safely lead 'Dead' sequences that your opponents can't interrupt.\n\nStuffed-Board Management: If the 'Pope' bowl hasn't been won for 5 rounds, it will be overflowing with chips. Players will bid and play much more aggressively to name Diamonds as trumps (if the variant allows bidding). In a standard game, if you hold the 9 of Diamonds and the board is 'Fat', your primary objective should be finding a way to lead Diamonds or interrupt a sequence to play itâ€”ignore the 'Game' bowl until the Pope is out.",
    Player: "Keep your 'Pope'! Save the 9 of Diamonds for a moment when an opponent is building a long sequence that you can't follow. By playing the Pope, you stop their momentum and get to lead a new sequence of your own. Also, pay attention to the trump suitâ€”winning the 'Matrimony' stake (King and Queen) is often more lucrative than finishing the round first.\n\nThe 'Stop Hand' Deduction: As cards are played, you can figure out what is in the face-down 'Stop Hand'. If a 5 of Spades is led and no one plays the 6, the 6 is definitely in the Stop Hand. This makes the 5 a permanent 'Stop' for the rest of the game. Use this knowledge to safely lead 'Dead' sequences that your opponents can't interrupt.\n\nStuffed-Board Management: If the 'Pope' bowl hasn't been won for 5 rounds, it will be overflowing with chips. Players will bid and play much more aggressively to name Diamonds as trumps (if the variant allows bidding). In a standard game, if you hold the 9 of Diamonds and the board is 'Fat', your primary objective should be finding a way to lead Diamonds or interrupt a sequence to play itâ€”ignore the 'Game' bowl until the Pope is out.",
